func=jag::packethandlers::ClientState::MINIMAP_FLAG_SET	func_addr=0x001aa9f0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=Identified by structural correspondence with the ELF's symbol-named MINIMAP_FLAG_SET: same GetWorldTranslation-into-this+0x168 opening, the same `this+0x1a9 \e (this+0x64 <\e cycle)` visibility latch behind the this+0x190 guard, the same AnimationWrapper at this+0x130 driven through its state at +0x18, the same this+0x148/0x150 -> this+0x158/0x160 shared_ptr swap, the same this+0xd0 model with its +0x170 threshold, and the same pair of draw calls behind the this+0x1a8 flag. This is the anchor the offset updater keys OGlobal.CLIENT off: the first RIP-relative load in the body is the g_client read that MSVC leaves here where gcc reaches the client through SceneManager::IsWorldReady.
func=jag::ClientStream::Write	func_addr=0x00639b50	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::ClientStream::Write(this, src, len) -> bytesWritten. Single funnel for ALL raw C->S bytes\n(already ISAAC-encrypted). Engine RawLoginDump hooks this for the raw login/RSA handshake.\nthis+0xe0 (byte) selects buffered mode: 0 \e immediate ws2_32 send(), non-0 \e append to the\npending vector (+0xc8 begin / +0xd0 end / +0xd8 cap) with grow-by-doubling, flushed by Flush.\nOn a short/failed send: Close + full ring reset.\nEvidence: (1) identical control flow and identical ClientStream field set to Linux\njag::ClientStream::Write; (2) calls ws2_32 send (Ordinal_19) + WSAGetLastError (Ordinal_111) where\nLinux calls send + __errno_location; (3) shares the bytes-written global _DAT_00e88a80 with Flush,\nexactly as the Linux pair shares its accumulator.
