func=jag::input::InputHandler::~InputHandler	func_addr=0x0078a880	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::input::InputHandler::~InputHandler. Destroys the 23 listener slots in reverse order\n(vector at 0x08 + n*0x68, mutex at +0x18 inside each), the 0x100-entry pointer-state vector at\n+0x968, the intrusive list at +0x980, and the refcounted pointer at +0x9b0. This is the function\nthat enumerates every slot, including 0x480 (slot 11) which RemoveAllListeners skips.
func=jag::ClientProt::SendEventMouseClick	func_addr=0x00111f00	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::ClientProt::SendEventMouseClick -- drains ONE MouseSample from MainLogicManager's CLICK ring and\nemits EVENT_MOUSE_CLICK. Returns immediately when read \e\e write. Called unconditionally each tick from\njag::ClientProt::FlushMouseProtSender (vtable slot 1).\n\nRing: base MainLogicManager+0x46f0 (reached here as [mlm+0x44c8] + (idx*5+0x45)*8), stride 0x28,\n50 slots, write cursor +0x4ec0, read cursor +0x4ec4. This function does NOT advance the read cursor --\nthe main-logic tick retires exactly one entry per tick (see the comment at 0x0010fa70). MainLogicManager\nalso owns a SEPARATE 200-slot MOVEMENT ring at +0x4ec8; see jag::ClientProt::PopEventMouseMoveSample.\n\nWire, 6 bytes, all little-endian:\n  [0..1] u16 sample->x clamped 0..0xffff\n  [2..3] u16 sample->y clamped 0..0xffff\n  [4..5] u16 (sample->timestamp - this->lastClickSampleTime) capped 0x7fff, OR (sample->button !\e 0) << 15\nOnly the low byte of the delta is written first, then (deltaHigh | buttonBit) -- so the button occupies\nbit 15 of the trailing LE short. Linux 949-4 registers this prot at opcode 2, size 6.\n\nsample->button IS A BUTTON IDENTIFIER, NOT A MOTION/CLICK DISCRIMINATOR. 0 means the LEFT button.\nEvidence: the per-tick minimenu/interaction update (FUN_00165150) sets its "left click pending" bool to\n(sample->button \e\e 0) when the ring is non-empty and to FALSE when the ring is EMPTY, while substituting\nthe live cursor position from MainLogicManager+0x46d8. Under a "0 \e\e motion sample" reading that\nassignment is self-contradictory (empty ring would mean "not a motion sample" while simultaneously\nfalling back to the live cursor); under "0 \e\e left button" it reads correctly as "no left click queued".\nThree independent consumers -- FUN_00165150, FUN_00162480 and the minimenu builder FUN_0016a5a0 --\nall use the queued sample as "where the click happened" and all fall back to the live cursor position\nwhen the ring is empty, which is only meaningful if the click ring is normally EMPTY. Motion therefore\ndoes not populate this ring; it populates the separate movement ring.\n\nCONSEQUENCE for synthetic input: a hand-written entry with button \e\e 0 does NOT produce a benign\n"cursor was here" report. It produces a well-formed EVENT_MOUSE_CLICK announcing a LEFT CLICK at those\ncoordinates. There is no encoding of this packet that means "moved without clicking" -- motion is\nreported only by the separate movement-history prot (descriptor DAT_00e8f600).\n\nNOT YET PROVEN: the producer that pushes into the click ring has not been located. No writer of the\nwrite cursor at +0x4ec0 exists anywhere in .text under any addressing form the consumers use\n(direct displacement 0x46f0/0x4ec0, the (idx*5+0x45)*8 idiom, or [mlm+0x44c8]+0x9f8), so the producer\nmust reach the ring through a pointer passed in or a shared push helper not yet identified. Until it is\nfound, the button\e\e0\e\eLEFT mapping rests on consumer semantics, not on a store of the constant.
func=jag::ClientProt::SendEventMouseClick	func_addr=0x00111f00	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=552	cu_index_from_entry=140	text=jag::Packet::SendClientMessage is INLINED here (and at every other call site) by MSVC -- there is\nno standalone Windows function for it, so OFunctions.SENDCLIENTMESSAGE has no Windows address.\nThe inlined body is the sequence from the freelist pop at conn+0x58 (pool +0x60/+0x68/+0x70) through\nthe intrusive-list push at conn+0x48/+0x50, the pending counter conn+0x88, packet+0x20 -> +0x28,\nand finally `add [conn+0x2b0], eax`. A scan for `01 8? b0 02 00 00` finds ~100 such sites, all\ninside larger sender functions and none at a function entry; jag::ConnectionManager::ProcessConnections\ncontains exactly two, matching the two SendClientMessage calls its Linux counterpart makes.
func=jag::ClientProt::SendNativeMouseClick	func_addr=0x00112300	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::ClientProt::SendNativeMouseClick(NativeMouseProt *this)\n\nWindows-only companion to SendEventMouseClick. Reports the OS's hardware-vs-injected verdict for one\nmouse-button event. Called UNCONDITIONALLY once per tick from jag::ClientProt::FlushMouseProtSender\n(vtable slot 1); it self-guards on ring emptiness and emits at most ONE packet per call.\n\nNAME PROVENANCE: SEND_NATIVE_MOUSE_CLICK is an official Jagex ClientProt name\n(re-resources/prot-names.json). The opcode/size descriptor pair at DAT_00e8f6c0 / DAT_00e8f6c4\nis populated at runtime by prot registration and is zero in the file, so the opcode CANNOT be read\nstatically -- any specific opcode number in older comments here was a guess and must not be trusted.\n\nRING (fully verified against producer jag::ClientProt::RecordNativeMouseButton and the ctor's\ninitialisation loop):\n  this->clickRing        base +0xa8,  NativeMouseSample stride 0x30, 10 slots (0xa8 + 10*0x30 \e 0x288)\n  this->clickRingWrite   +0x288  producer cursor\n  this->clickRingRead    +0x28c  consumer cursor, advanced by THIS function after a send\n  empty test: clickRingRead \e\e clickRingWrite  (identical shape to the MainLogicManager click ring)\nFields consumed: sample->x (+0x04 float), sample->y (+0x08 float), sample->timestamp (+0x18 int64),\nsample->message (+0x28 int32 \e RAW WM_* number, not an abstract enum), sample->sourceFlags (+0x2c\nint32 \e MSLLHOOKSTRUCT.flags, only bit 0 / LLMHF_INJECTED reaches the wire).\n\nWIRE, 7 bytes:\n  [0]    0x80 | ((message & 0x7f) << 1) | (sourceFlags & 1)\n  [1..2] BE u16 (sample->timestamp - this->base.lastClickSampleTime), capped 0xffff;\n         lastClickSampleTime is then overwritten with sample->timestamp (no clock read at send time)\n  [3..4] BE u16 x, clamped 0..0xffff\n  [5..6] BE u16 y, clamped 0..0xffff\nFor the messages the LL hook forwards (WM_LBUTTONDOWN 0x201 .. WM_MBUTTONDBLCLK 0x209) the low byte\nof message is 1..9, so byte[0] lands in 0x82..0x92.\n\nProducer is jag::ClientProt::RecordNativeMouseButton, reached from\njag::input::EventListeners::DispatchMouseEventWithSource. Emitting EVENT_MOUSE_CLICK without this\npacket leaves a click with no source report. Linux registers the prot but never sends it -- there is\nno user32 low-level hook to source it from.
