func=jag::ProjectileList::Add	func_addr=0x0019de60	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::ProjectileList::Add - appends a projectile. this+0x8 \e jag::Client*.\nList fields: +0x10 head sentinel, +0x18 tail, +0x20/+0x28/+0x30/+0x38 node pool/freelist,\n+0x50 live count (hard cap 100 - the oldest is evicted first).\nPooled ProjectileEntity stride 0x1C0; construction is FUN_001a8d50 (the ProjectileEntity ctor,\nwhich calls jag::game::Entity::Entity). GraphNode+0x1A0 is set to the new entity (back-ptr).\nOClient.SCENE_MANAGER \e 0x19990 on Windows: client[0x19990] is the SceneManager, and\nGetActiveWorld is inlined here as `idx \e sm[0x70]; world \e sm[0x58] + idx*0x10` (shared_ptr array),\nbailing to the null-world singleton when idx \e\e -1.\nEvidence: (1) the `count \e\e 100` eviction guard and the identical intrusive-list/freelist field\nset; (2) the 0x1C0 pool element stride, identical to Linux; (3) the same 19-argument signature and\nthe same tail (push node, bump count, write the entity back-ptr into GraphNode+0x1A0).
func=jag::input::Input::OnLeftButtonUp	func_addr=0x0078b700	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::input::Input::OnLeftButtonUp(Input* this, float x, float y).\nReached from the Win32 message dispatch FUN_0078a2f0 case 0x202 (WM_LBUTTONUP) at 0x0078a587.\nClears LEFT_BUTTON_STATE (0x00e8e4f4) \e 0, publishes MOUSE_Y/MOUSE_X, dispatches the LMOUSE_UP\nslot via FUN_00789470 (handler+0x70 begin / +0x78 end / +0x88 mutex).\nProves OInputHandler.LMOUSE_UP \e 0x70.\nLinux counterpart jag::input::Input::OnLeftButtonUp .
func=jag::graphics::GraphNode::GraphNode	func_addr=0x004c2b00	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::graphics::GraphNode::GraphNode (Windows). Field-for-field identical to the Linux 949-4 ctor\n at EVERY offset - the whole GraphNode layout can be ported 1:1:\n  0x00..0x3f  zeroed 4x4 world transform matrix (GetWorldTransformationMatrixAligned  writes\n              its rows at 0x00/0x10/0x20/0x30 and the translation at 0x30/0x34/0x38 with 1.0f at 0x3c)\n              \e> OGraphNode.DIRECTION_X/Y/Z \e 0x0/0x8/0x10 are matrix elements m00/m02/m10\n  0x40/0x44/0x48 \e +FLT_MAX, 0x4c pad ; 0x50/0x54/0x58 \e -FLT_MAX, 0x5c \e -1.0f   (transformed AABB)\n  0x60..0x7f     same sentinels                                                    (source AABB)\n  0x80..0xbf     world matrix scratch ; 0xd0/0xd4/0xd8 local pos (0xdc \e 4th slot of that qword pair)\n  0xec \e 1.0f ; 0xf4/0xf8 \e 0 ; 0xfc flags (0xc7 / 0xe7)\n  0x100/0x104/0x108 \e 1.0f scale ; 0x130 parent ; 0x138/0x140/0x158 child vector -> &node+0x160\n  0x148 -> &node+0x1a0 ; 0x1a0 entity back-ptr \e 0\n  0x1a8/0x1b0/0x1b8/0x1c0/0x1c8 \e -1  (so 0x1ac, the engine's FRAME_COUNT, is a -1-seeded int here)\n  0x1d0 \e 0 ; word 0x1d8 \e 0 ; 0x1e0/0x1e8/0x200 dirty-listener vector -> &node+0x208 ; 0x1f0 -> &node+0x210
func=jag::Client::DiscardPendingInput	func_addr=0x00027d40	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::Client::DiscardPendingInput(client) -- drops all queued input without consuming it. Drains BOTH\nMainLogicManager mouse rings by copying each write cursor into its read cursor:\n  click ring     read +0x4ec4 \e write +0x4ec0\n  movement ring  read +0x6e0c \e write +0x6e08\nand additionally a third ring pair at +0x6e08-adjacent... (no: the third pair drained here is the\nkey/char ring). Also clears the live button-state bytes at +0x46e8..+0x46ea and the pending-target\nfield at +0x74e8.\n\nThe presence of two independent write/read cursor pairs being reset side by side is the second\nindependent confirmation (after the MainLogicManager constructor's two init loops and\njag::ClientProt::PopEventMouseMoveSample) that the click ring and the movement ring are distinct\nbuffers, not two views of one.
