func=jag::NPCList::GetNPCNode	func_addr=0x000b7090	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::NPCList::GetNPCNode(this, npcIndex) - hash lookup of a local NPC by its server index.\nBucket array at this+0x10, bucket count at this+0x18, node \e { int key; ...; next @ +0x18 },\nmapped shared_ptr<NPC> at node+8 (refcount @ +0, object @ +8). Returns node+8, or the\nnot-found sentinel DAT_00e9e6b0.\n\nSymbol is exact, taken from Linux 949-5 jag::NPCList::GetNPCNode: identical algorithm with\nidentical member offsets (bucket array +0x10, bucket count +0x18, key at node+0, next at\nnode+0x18, returns node+8, single sentinel return). The Linux function is called with\nthis \e [client + 0x194b8] \e Linux OClient.NPC_MANAGER; the Windows callers pass\n[client + 0x198f0].
