func=jag::ConnectionManager::TcpIn	func_addr=0x000e94c0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::ConnectionManager::TcpIn(ConnectionManager*, ServerConnectionSlot*) - CERTAIN.\nInbound packet pump. Guards on four empty-queue checks against the object at Client+0x19940, then\nloops at most 100 times calling FUN_000e9540 (the per-packet read/dispatch body) until it returns\nfalse.\nEvidence (3 independent):\n 1. Guard is byte-identical in shape to the Linux TcpIn guard and uses the SAME four field pairs\n    inside the guarded object (0x190A20/0x190A28, 0x190A50/0x190A58, 0x190A80/0x190A88,\n    0x190AB0/0x190AB8) - same class, same layout.\n 2. Same 100-iteration bounded pump.\n 3. Called from ProcessConnections (0x000e8f30) as TcpIn(this, this+0x20) for the game connection\n    and TcpIn(this, this+0x10) for the lobby connection - exactly the two call sites and slot\n    offsets the Linux ProcessConnections uses.\nThe per-packet body FUN_000e9540 (outlined on MSVC, inlined on GCC) works on the ServerConnection\nat slot+8 with the same field offsets as Linux: currentOpcode +0x2C, resolvedSize +0x30,\nisaac +0x2B8, packet +0x2C0, retry counters +0x38/+0x3C, lastOpcode +0x2E0.
