func=jag::Client::SetMainState	func_addr=0x00026eb0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::Client::SetMainState(Client*, int newState) - CERTAIN.\nStructural 1:1 with the Linux jag::Client::SetMainState: read mainState int; return if unchanged;\nwalk the listener vector backwards from end to begin invoking listener vtable[+8](listener,\noldState, newState); then store newState.\nWindows layout read out of this function: mainState \e int @ Client+0x19F60, listener vector\nbegin @ Client+0x19818, end @ Client+0x19820.\nCross-checks: Client+0x19F60 is initialised to 0 in the ctor (jag::Client::Client, store to\nparam_1[0x33EC]); it is the value ConnectionManager::ProcessConnections switches on (0x14/0x17/\n0x1E) and the value this function is called to change (SetMainState(client,10),\nSetMainState(client,0x23) on disconnect) - the same call sites the Linux DB records.
