func=jag::input::Input::OnKeyCharInner	func_addr=0x00034260	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=The `if (*(char *)(this + 0xc8) \e\e 0)` guard at the top is the Linux jag::input::Input::OnKeyChar\nwrapper (0x002e8990) inlined into the Inner: `if (this->consoleKeyHeld) return;`.\nSo Input+0xc8 is BOTH the engine's OInput.CONSOLE_KEY_HELD (Linux 0x98) and the field already\nrecorded as OInput.CONSOLE_OPEN_FLAG -- one and the same byte on Windows. It is set by\nOnKeyDownInner's 0x1ca3 path and cleared by OnKeyUpInner on vk 0x1ca3.\nWindows has no separate outer OnKeyChar; the vtable+0x18 slot points straight here.
func=jag::WorldLobbyData::GetHTTPURL	func_addr=0x0012a6b0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=Builds the "scheme://host:port" content URL for a world or lobby endpoint. Windows counterpart of the Linux jag::WorldLobbyData::GetHTTPURL.\n\nScheme and port selection: when the ClientParameters TLS flag is set it emits https:// with the explicitly configured secure port; otherwise it emits http:// and picks the live literal content port if the server profile is the live/default one, else derives the port by adding a per-server-type base constant to the world id.\n\nRegister use differs from the Linux build: the WorldLobbyData is the first integer argument and the caller-supplied string buffer is the second, rather than the sret-first order the Itanium ABI gives the Linux build.
func=jag::WorldLobbyData::GetHTTPURL	func_addr=0x0012a6b0	kind=plate	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=Setting prototype: eastl_fixed_string_256 * GetHTTPURL(WorldLobbyData * this, eastl_fixed_string_256 * result)
func=jag::WorldLobbyData::GetHTTPURL	func_addr=0x0012a6b0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=82	cu_index_from_entry=20	text=Project X patcher target: the live-mode HTTP content port literal. Used when the ClientParameters TLS flag is clear and the server profile is the live/default one; the runtime patcher rewrites this immediate with the port from PROJECTX_HTTP_PORT.\n\nHow the patcher locates it: by the pair of world-port base constants this same basic block adds to the world id, not by the surrounding opcode bytes. Those differ between compilers, between builds, and between the Linux build's two copies of this logic.\n\nSite count is platform-specific and must be re-checked every build. This MSVC build keeps GetHTTPURL out of line and reaches it only through direct calls, so this is its only occurrence; the Linux build of the same revision additionally inlines the whole body into jag::ClientCrashReportingDataProvider::GetAddress and needs both copies patched.
