func=jag::game::Camera::ForceAngle	func_addr=0x00191200	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::game::Camera::ForceAngle(this, pitchX, yawY) - installs an absolute camera orientation.\nSelects the active camera controller (this+0x2a0, or this+0x98 when the mode vfunc at\nvtbl+0x18 returns 6); when the controller's vfunc at vtbl+0xd8 reports clamping is enabled,\nclamps pitchX into [0x80,0x180] and wraps yawY modulo 0x800. Builds the orientation from\n(pitchX*8, (0x400 - yawY)*8) and applies it through the controller vfunc at vtbl+0xb0, then\nsets the camera-dirty flag at this+0x5c8.\n\nClass name is symbol-derived: Linux 949-5 jag::game::Camera::ProcessCameraReset is called\nwith this \e [client + 0x19420], the Linux OClient.CAMERA field, i.e. the same object this\nmethod receives from Windows [client + 0x19858]. The method name ForceAngle is descriptive,\nnot a recovered symbol: the only two callers are jag::opcode::cam_forceangle and\njag::PacketHandlers::CamForceangle.
