func=jag::game::InterfaceComponent::ComputeOriginOffset	func_addr=0x00269830	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::game::InterfaceComponent::ComputeOriginOffset — Windows counterpart of Linux 0x411910. Switches on the origin-mode bytes and emits {xOff, yOff, xFrac, yFrac} into the out-param.\nProves OInterfaceComponent X_ORIGIN_MODE\e0x32, Y_ORIGIN_MODE\e0x33, X_ORIGIN_OFFSET\e0x38, Y_ORIGIN_OFFSET\e0x3c (all identical to Linux), and re-confirms SCREEN_WIDTH\e0x58 / SCREEN_HEIGHT\e0x5c.
func=jag::hal::JagRenderViewProc	func_addr=0x00728670	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=WndProc for window class "JagRenderView" (registered by jag::hal::RegisterJagRenderViewClass\n, lpfnWndProc at WNDCLASSEXA+0x08 - NOT +0x10).\nTHIS IS THE WINDOWS INPUT ENTRY POINT. The client uses TWO window classes:\n  "JagWindow"     -> jag::hal::JagWindowProc  - top-level frame. Handles ONLY window\n                     management (WM_NCCREATE 0x81, WM_DESTROY 3, WM_SIZE 5, WM_SETFOCUS 7,\n                     WM_CLOSE 0x10, WM_GETMINMAXINFO 0x24, WM_COMMAND 0x111,\n                     WM_ENTERSIZEMOVE/EXITSIZEMOVE 0x231/0x232). NO keyboard or mouse messages.\n                     It forwards focus and sizing to the child HWND at frame[0xe0]->[0x20].\n  "JagRenderView" -> this - the child render/input window; receives all WM_KEY*/WM_CHAR/WM_MOUSE*.\nThis function only stashes the owner at GWLP_USERDATA on WM_NCCREATE, registers device\nnotification (DBT_DEVTYP_DEVICEINTERFACE, 0x20-byte filter), then tail-calls the real handler\nFUN_00728830(owner, hwnd, msg, wParam, lParam) - which is where the WM_KEYDOWN/WM_MOUSEMOVE/\nWM_MOUSEWHEEL dispatch into jag::input::Input::On* lives. NOT YET ANALYSED.\nFrame-object fields seen here and in JagWindowProc: +0xe0 child-view wrapper (HWND at +0x20),\n+0xe8/+0xec client width/height as float, +0x148/+0x14c min size, +0x238 resize-dirty flag,\n+0x23c dpi scale numerator, +0x240 own HWND, +0x289 in-size-move flag.
