func=jag::EventListeners::CallListeners	func_addr=0x00789410	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::EventListeners<std::function<bool(float,float)>>::CallListeners(inputHandler, x, y) -> bool.\nLocks the slot mutex at handler+0x290, walks the listener vector handler+0x278 (begin) ..\nhandler+0x280 (end), and for each non-null element invokes\n    callable \e *(void**)(*element + 0x38);\n    (*(code**)(*callable + 0x10))(callable, &x, &y);\nreturning 1 on the first listener that returns true, 0 if none consumed.\nNOTE the argument order is (&x, &y) - x first. Same std::function shape as the DoAction\ncallables: engaged pointer at +0x38, invoke at vtable slot 2 (+0x10).\nInputHandler listener-slot layout (derived, NOT the Linux 0x08 + n*0x40):\n    slot n at 0xd8 + n*0x68; within a slot: +0x00 begin, +0x08 end, +0x10 cap, +0x18 mutex.\n    slot 0  \e 0xd8  middle-button-down (walked inline by the WndProc dispatch)\n    slot 4  \e 0x278 mouse-motion (this function)\n    slot 17 \e 0x7c0 device-change (WM_DEVICECHANGE)\nEvidence: (1) identical iterate-and-stop-on-true contract to the Linux CallListeners;\n(2) the 0x68 slot stride is exact across all three observed slots ((0x278-0xd8)/0x68 \e 4,\n(0x7c0-0xd8)/0x68 \e 17) with the mutex consistently +0x18 inside the slot; (3) reached from\njag::input::Input::OnMouseMotion for every named handler and for the global handler.
func=jag::InterfaceManager::IfButtonXInner	func_addr=0x00170860	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=InterfaceComponent field evidence (componentRef[1] is the component): +0x8 ushort interfaceId, +0xa ushort componentId, +0xc ushort slotId, each 0xffff \e none. Packed as (interfaceId &lt;&lt; 16 | componentId) in the low dword of the CS2 hook arg with (slotId + 1) in the high dword. +0x68 \e hook table (hook id 0x27 looked up here). +0x130 \e eastl::string text (SSO marker at +0x147, heap size at +0x138); empty text selects the IF_BUTTON1..10 path, non-empty selects the with-text packet which also carries the byte at +0x148. CAUTION: +0xe is NOT a component field - the +0xe reads in FUN_00169e40 / FUN_0016fe20 are on a different struct (reached via component+0x100, or via a shared_ptr pointee) where +0x8 is an interface id and +0xe a slot index into a 0x18-stride array.
