func=jag::game::PlayerVarDomain::SetVarValue	func_addr=0x002e9480	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::game::PlayerVarDomain::setBit(this, varInfo, variant).\nSame shape as ::set but writes the SECOND value map at this+0x1c0c8, additionally stores -1 to\nthis+0x39608, and inserts into the dirty map with flag 0 (::set uses flag 1).\nEvidence: (1) the this+0x1c0c8 map is used by no other method and is the exact map Linux\n::setBit uses; (2) the scalar -1 write is present only in ::setBit on both platforms;\n(3) identical dirty-map insert but with the opposite flag value, matching the Linux pair.
