func=jag::input::Input::OnMouseMotion	func_addr=0x0078ba90	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::input::Input::OnMouseMotion(input, x, y). Free function, `this` \e the jag::input::Input the\nWndProc dispatch (FUN_0078a2d0) is invoked on.\njag::input::Input layout (derived here and cross-checked against the dispatch):\n    +0x08 globalHandler (InputHandler*)   +0x18 mLock (mutex)\n    +0x68 namedHandlers rbtree anchor     +0x70 rbtree begin; node value at node+0x38\n    +0xb0 mouseX          +0xb4 mouseY\n    +0xb8 consoleKey vk (dispatch compares the incoming vk against it and pre-fires 0x1ca3)\n    vtable +0x08 OnKeyDown, +0x10 OnKeyUp, +0x18 OnKeyChar  <-- RVAs STILL UNRESOLVED\nWalks the named-handler rbtree calling CallListeners(handlerValue, x, y), stops on the first\nhandler that consumes, then falls through to the global handler. Publishes the final position to\njag::input::InputState::MOUSE_X/MOUSE_Y - and only writes them when NO listener consumed the\nevent (the consumed path keeps the previously latched values).\nWARNING for the next session: the vtable at 0x00b5a690 whose slots +0x8/+0x10/+0x18 are\n0x0078c5b0 / 0x0078c940 / 0x0078c7c0 is NOT this class's vtable. 0x0078c5b0 decompiles as a\ntouch/pointer-down handler taking (this, ?, pointerId, x, y) that reaches the Input indirectly via\nthis+0x70 and dispatches through FUN_00789900 (the 3-arg listener form). Do not use those three\naddresses as the keyboard handlers.
