func=jag::game::ServerConnection::ReadIncomingMessage	func_addr=0x000ff0d0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::game::ServerConnection::ReadIncomingMessage(ServerConnection* conn, shared_ptr<TcpConnectionMessage>* out)\n\nWINDOWS ServerConnection field map (all derived from THIS function's own code, no Linux import):\n  +0x08  ClientStream*      -- passed as `this` to ClientStream::Read/GetAvailable at 7 call sites\n  +0x2C  currentOpcode      (int, -1 \e none)\n  +0x30  resolvedSize       (int, -1 \e g1 var, -2 \e g2 var, else fixed)\n  +0x34  opcodeHalfRead     (bool)\n  +0x35  payloadReady       (bool)\n  +0x38/+0x3C stall counters\n  +0x2B8 Isaac*\n  +0x2C0 Packet             (handed to the prot handler as arg 1 by FUN_000e9540)\n  +0x2D0 Packet.data        (u8*) -- the DESTINATION buffer of every ClientStream::Read here\n  +0x2D8 Packet.pos         (u64) -- zeroed before each Read, +\e bytesRead, then indexed as data[pos]\n  +0x2E0 lastOpcode\n  +0x2E8 total byte counter\n\nPacket-relative: PACKET_BASE 0x2C0 \e> data at Packet+0x10, pos at Packet+0x18.\nSame layout holds on TcpConnectionMessage (Packet at msg+0x08 \e> data msg+0x18, pos msg+0x20).\n\nTail inlines TcpConnectionMessage::InitIncoming: pool element stride 0x60, control block at\nelem+0x00 (vtable PTR_FUN_00b572d0, strong +0x08, weak +0x0C), message object at elem+0x20.\nWrites prot back-ptr at msg+0x38 then the plain (non-ISAAC) opcode byte at data[pos++].
