func=jag::game::PlayerVarDomain::SetVarValueFromServer	func_addr=0x002e9580	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::game::PlayerVarDomain::set(this, varInfo, variant) - the varp write chokepoint.\nthis lives at jag::Client + 0x19F78 (OClient.PLAYER_VAR_DOMAIN).\nkey \e varInfo->[+0x8]->[+0x8] (varInfo -> VarType -> var id).\nValue map at this+0x20 (FindOrCreateEntry, variant stored at entry+0x8).\nDirty map at this+0x38170 (buckets +0x38178, bucketCount +0x38180): if the id is already present\nand not yet flagged, stamp node+0x8 with the cycle and set node+0x10 \e 1; otherwise insert\n{cycle, 1}. The per-tick drain pushes these ids into the ring on client[0x19958].\nEvidence: (1) identical key derivation and identical two-map structure to Linux\njag::game::PlayerVarDomain::set, including the same this+0x20 value map and this+0x38170 dirty map;\n(2) called by the VARP ServerProt handlers with client+0x19F78 - the same domain the CS2 var\nopcodes pass; (3) its sibling setBit uses the second map and flag 0, exactly the Linux split.
