func=jag::PacketHandlers::UpdateInvFull	func_addr=0x000fc020	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::PacketHandlers::UpdateInvFull - handler+0x0 \e jag::Client*.\nWire: g2 inventoryId, g1 flags (bit0 \e secondary, bit1 \e per-slot vars follow), then\nCreateInventory(client[0x19988], id, flags&1) - a full snapshot always replaces the inventory,\nso unlike UpdateInvPartial there is no GetInventory lookup. Then g2 slotCount and exactly\nslotCount sequential entries (no per-entry slot index, which is the whole difference from\nUpdateInvPartial): count \e (g_protocolRevision < 0x3B5 ? g2 : g3), objId \e g1 with 0xFF -> g4,\nand if (flags&2) varCount \e g1 followed by varCount * (g2 varId, g4 value).\nTail: same dirty-inventory ring on client[0x19958] (+0xa8 / +0xb0) and the same sentinel return.\nEvidence: (1) the only caller of CreateInventory besides UpdateInvPartial; (2) byte-identical\nentry decode ladder, protocol-revision gate and var loop shared with UpdateInvPartial;\n(3) sequential-slot iteration bounded by a leading g2 count - the exact Full-vs-Partial contrast\npresent in the Linux pair - plus the identical dirty-ring tail and sentinel return.
