func=jag::game::ClientError::ReportError	func_addr=0x003f7c50	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::game::ClientError::ReportError(configProvider**, char* message, uint* stackTrace, flags).\nCrash/error telemetry funnel. Builds\n  "%s/nxtclienterror.w3>clientToken\e%s&timeStamp\e%llu&c\e%d&cs\e%d&nxt\e%s&u\e%s&cid\e%d&devbuild\e%d"\nfrom vtable getters on *param_1: +0x08 nxt version, +0x10 user, +0x18 cid, +0x20 clientToken,\n+0x30 port, +0x38 payload prefix, +0x40 cs, +0x48 c. Serialises the message plus, when\n(flags & 1) and stackTrace !\e null, a frame array - each frame rebased to a module-relative RVA\nvia GetModuleHandleA(NULL) - then urlencodes the blob into a "data\e" body and posts it.\n(flags & 4) routes to FUN_003f8230 first (dedupe / already-reported check) and suppresses the send.\nEvidence: (1) sole referencer of the telemetry format string ; (2) the vtable getters it\ncalls line up field-for-field with the query parameters that string names; (3) the frame-to-RVA\nrebasing plus "data\e" body is the crash-report shape of the Linux jag::game::ClientError::ReportError.\nThe engine hooks this to suppress telemetry.
