func=jag::graphics::GraphNode::UpdateBounds	func_addr=0x004c3e60	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::graphics::GraphNode::UpdateBounds (Windows). MSVC outlined what GCC merged into the Linux\nflag-propagation walk  (branch at 0x788b30) - identical instruction-for-instruction:\n  TEST byte [node+0xfc],8            bounds-dirty flag\n  MOVUPS [node+0x40] <- [node+0x60]  transformed AABB min  <- source AABB min\n  MOVUPS [node+0x50] <- [node+0x70]  transformed AABB max  <- source AABB max\n  then GetWorldTransformationMatrixAligned + transform-in-place on node+0x40, and node+0x60 -> node+0x80\n\e> OGraphNode.BOUNDS_MIN_X/Z/Y \e 0x40/0x44/0x48 and BOUNDS_MAX_X/Z/Y \e 0x50/0x54/0x58, identical to Linux.\nThe GraphNode ctor  independently seeds 0x40/0x44/0x48 \e +FLT_MAX, 0x50/0x54/0x58 \e -FLT_MAX,\n0x5c \e -1.0f - byte-identical to the Linux ctor .
func=jag::Client::ResetEntityManagers	func_addr=0x00027510	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=Re-fires every entity manager's main-state-changed listener and detaches all per-entity\nscene attachments. Called from the region-rebuild paths (REBUILD_NORMAL, REBUILD_REGION)\nand from the scene-teardown wrapper FUN_00027740.\n\nFor SPOTANIM (Client+0x19948), PROJECTILE (+0x19920), ITEMSTACK (+0x198f8, +0x50\nsubobject), HINTTRAIL (+0x198b8), +0x198b0 and +0x19890 it invokes vtable slot +8 with\n(mainState, mainState) - the same listener slot jag::Client::SetMainState drives with\n(oldState, newState), and the same mainState int at Client+0x19f60. The overrides purge\nthe manager's collections.\nFor PLAYER_MANAGER (+0x19910) it walks the active-index int vector (+0x4038/+0x4040) into\nthe slot table (+0x10); for NPCList (+0x198f0) it walks the id array (+0xa0a0, count\n+0xb0a0) through jag::NPCList::GetNPCNode. Each entity is passed to an inplace-functor\n(vtables PTR_LAB_00b5e628 / PTR_LAB_00b5e6b8) that nulls and releases the attachment\nvectors at entity+0x1018/+0x1020 (and +0x1038/+0x1040 for players) and drops the\nshared_ptr at entity+0x48.\n\nFunction identity and behaviour are certain; the NAME is descriptive, not a recovered\nsymbol - the Linux counterpart FUN_00293200 (called from jag::PacketHandlers::RebuildNormal\nimmediately before the store to [client+0x194b8]+0xc0e0) is unnamed there too.
