func=jag::input::DispatchLowLevelMouseMessage	func_addr=0x00729240	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::input::DispatchLowLevelMouseMessage(hookState, message, MSLLHOOKSTRUCT *)\n\nBody of the WH_MOUSE_LL hook. param_3 is an MSLLHOOKSTRUCT, so param_3[1].y is its `flags` field --\nthis is where MSLLHOOKSTRUCT.flags (bit 0 \e LLMHF_INJECTED) enters the client.\n\nFilters first: returns immediately for 0x2a0/0x2a2 and the 0xa0..0xad WM_NC* range; converts the screen\npoint to client coordinates via GetClientRect + ClientToScreen and drops anything outside the client\nrect or not over the game window (WindowFromPoint).\n\nThen, for each InputHandler in the red-black tree at (hookState+0xf8 -> vtable+0x50) plus the single\nhandler at that container+0x8:\n  message 0x200 (WM_MOUSEMOVE)                       -> DispatchMouseMoveWithSource\n  messages 0x201 0x203 0x204 0x206 0x207 0x209       -> DispatchMouseEventWithSource\n  anything else                                      -> not dispatched at all\nNote the absence of the *BUTTONUP messages (0x202/0x205/0x208): a physical press produces exactly one\nnative button sample, and a double-click produces two (DOWN then DBLCLK).
func=jag::MiniMenu::RegisterComponentDoActions	func_addr=0x000e06a0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=Second DoAction registration function (sibling of jag::MiniMenu::RegisterDoActions );\nboth are called back-to-back from jag::MiniMenu::MiniMenu , and those two calls are the\nONLY registration sites - so the complete DoAction set for this build is 7 here + 59 there \e 66.\n\nRegisters the interface-component family, which RegisterDoActions does not touch. Same object\nlayout: +0x00 callable vtable, +0x08 captured jag::Client*, +0x38 engaged ptr, +0x40 id, +0x44 kind.\nSender \e callable vtable +0x10.\n\n  action base  vtable   sender    id    kind\n  c69ff0       b597d8   01c190    1006  0     (sender sits outside the 0x10ad70-0x10bc30 band)\n  c6a110       b59748   10bc30    1005  0\n  c6a8b0       b59718   10bbf0      25  1     DoOpTargetComponent\n  c6a910       b597a8   10bbb0      30  1     DoOpDialog\n  c6a970       b59778   10bb70      57  1     DoOpComponent\n  c6a9c0    (copy c6a970) 10bb70   1007  1     DoOpComponent  - shares 57's callable\n  c69f80       b59688   10bb30      58  1     DoOpTargetComponentItem\n\nid 1007 copying id 57's callable is independently corroborated by the older Linux build, where\nCOMPONENT(57) and COMPONENT_SIXPLUS(1007) both resolve to the same address.
