func=jag::game::HintTrail::BuildFromPacket	func_addr=0x001a1440	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=HINT_TRAIL (ServerProt, SERVER, opcode 29) trail-point builder - the MSVC counterpart of the ELF jag::game::HintTrail::BuildFromPacket, which does the entity creation and the point walk in one function while the PE splits creation into EnsureSlotEntity.\n\nConfirms the HintTrail entity layout is IDENTICAL to the ELF build (same 0x14b0 alloc, same field indices):\n  +0x70 pointsBegin, +0x78 pointsEnd, +0x80 pointsCapacity (fixed_vector, inline storage at +0x98)\n  point stride 0x28 (loop steps 'lVar12 + 0x28'; last point read as pointsEnd - 0x28)\n  point +0x08 fineX, +0x0c height, +0x10 fineY - as (tile * 0x200) + 0x100\n\nNote for anchoring: MSVC merges the X and height writes into one 64-bit store\n(puVar9[1] \e CONCAT44(0xbf800000, fineX)), so unlike the ELF build there is NO\n'MOV dword [point+0xc], 0xBF800000' instruction to key an anchor on.
