func=jag::game::PathingEntity::AddHeadbar	func_addr=0x003243e0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=OPathingEntity.HITMARKS_AND_HEADBARS \e 0xf08 on Windows (Linux 949-4 \e 0xef8, so +0x10).\nThree independent Windows sites:\n  0x32443a  MOV RCX,[entity+0xf08]  here (AddHeadbar -> jag::HitmarksAndHeadbars::AddHeadbar)\n  0x3243de  MOV RCX,[entity+0xf08]  in AddHitmark \n  0x3242f5  LEA RAX,[entity+0xf08]  in ResetHitmarksAndHeadbars  - the unique_ptr slot the\n            0x40-byte HitmarksAndHeadbars object is stored into / freed from.\nLinux counterpart: MOV R11,[R13+0xef8]  inside jag::PlayerEntity::ProcessExtendedInfo.\nAlso confirms OPathingEntity.CONFIG_PROVIDER \e 0x78 (passed as arg2 of both Add* forwarders).\nThe offset table's current Windows value 0xffffffffffffff98 is garbage and must be replaced with 0xf08.
func=jag::input::Input::OnLeftButtonDown	func_addr=0x0078b5e0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::input::Input::OnLeftButtonDown(Input* this, float x, float y).\nReached from the Win32 message dispatch FUN_0078a2f0 case 0x201 (WM_LBUTTONDOWN) at 0x0078a54c,\nafter SetFocus/SetCapture, with XMM1 \e LOWORD(lParam) as x and XMM2 \e HIWORD(lParam) as y.\nSets jag::input::InputState::LEFT_BUTTON_STATE (0x00e8e4f4) \e 1 at 0x0078b731, publishes\nMOUSE_Y (0x00e8e4c0) / MOUSE_X (0x00e8e4c4), then walks the named-handler rbtree\n(anchor this+0x68, begin this+0x70, value at node+0x38) calling the LMOUSE_DOWN slot dispatcher\nFUN_007893b0, stopping on the first handler that consumes, then falls through to the global\nhandler at this+0x08.\nProves OInputHandler.LMOUSE_DOWN \e 0x8 (via FUN_007893b0 which reads handler+0x8/+0x10, mutex +0x20)\nand OInputGlobals.LEFT_BUTTON_STATE \e 0xe8e4f4.\nLinux counterpart jag::input::Input::OnLeftButtonDown .
func=jag::game::World::World	func_addr=0x002f6a10	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::game::World::World(...). Installs the World vtable, takes the four build-area mapsquare bounds as trailing stack arguments and stores them in offset order, installs the embedded HeightMap and LinkMap vtables, and stores the World back-pointer into the HeightMap subobject. Returns `this`. This store sequence is the field map for the OWorld mapsquare/heightmap band.
func=jag::game::AnimationWrapper::EmitFrameEvents	func_addr=0x002f0de0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=Walks the frames played since the last tick and fires the wrapper's per-frame event callback for each. [this+0x24] is the frame cursor the engine exposes as OAnimation.CURRENT_FRAME; it is compared against the playback state's counter at [[this+0x18]+0x98] and written back on every return path. gcc inlines this whole loop into AnimationWrapper::Update.
