func=jag::ClientProt::NativeMouseClickPending	func_addr=0x00112600	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::ClientProt::NativeMouseClickPending -- vtable slot 0 of the NATIVE mouse sender, the\n"is there work" predicate FlushMouseProtSender consults before building the movement-history packet.\n\n  if (clickRingRead !\e clickRingWrite) return true;              // a native button sample is queued\n  return (clock 0x00e8e498 - base.lastMoveSampleTime) > 0x7d0;   // else: history is stale enough\n\nIt does NOT gate the click send -- FlushMouseProtSender tail-calls slot 1 regardless of this result.\njag::ClientProt::EventMouseClickPending is the byte-for-byte analogue for the EVENT sender, testing the\nMainLogicManager click ring (base +0x46f0, stride 0x28, 50 slots, cursors +0x4ec0 write / +0x4ec4 read)\nagainst the same clock and the same 0x7d0 threshold. Both rings therefore use the identical\nread !\e write emptiness test.
