func=jag::game::TcpConnectionMessage::Init	func_addr=0x0008c120	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::game::TcpConnectionMessage::Init(msg, protOpcode, protSize) - shared body of the Linux\nInit / InitIncoming pair (which are byte-identical clones there; MSVC emitted one copy and\ninlined the differing tail at each of the 3 call sites).\nmsg: +0x0 protOpcode, +0x4 protSize, +0x10/+0x18/+0x20 Packet(begin/data/pos), +0x28 flag,\n+0x58 prot back-ptr (written by the caller).\nBuffer capacity ladder, byte-identical to Linux: size\e\e-1 -> 0x104, size\e\e-2 -> 10000,\nsize<0x13 -> 0x14, size<99 -> 0x62, else 0x104.\nThe tail the callers inline: store prot back-ptr, then write the opcode byte - ISAAC-added\nwhen an Isaac* is supplied (outgoing), plain pT<unsigned_char> otherwise (incoming).\nEvidence: (1) identical capacity constant ladder incl. the 0x12/99 boundaries; (2) identical\nfield writes and the same allocate/swap/free-old buffer dance; (3) reached from the incoming\nread path FUN_000ff0c0 exactly where Linux TcpIn calls InitIncoming.
