func=jag::ClientProt::FlushPerTick	func_addr=0x001112c0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::ClientProt::FlushPerTick(clientProt) -- the ClientProt aggregate's once-per-tick outbound pump,\ncalled from the MainLogicManager main-logic tick (client+0x19870 is the aggregate). Runs only when\nclient main state \e\e 0x1e (in-game) AND connection state \e\e 2.\n\nFirst two calls are the mouse senders, in this order:\n  FlushMouseProtSender(clientProt + 0x10)   EVENT mouse sender  (SendEventMouseClick)\n  FlushMouseProtSender(clientProt + 0x38)   NATIVE mouse sender (SendNativeMouseClick)\nso a tick that has both a queued game click and a queued native sample emits the EVENT packet before\nthe NATIVE one. Remaining work in this function: a batched key/interface-event packet, a camera-angle\npacket, a window-focus packet (edge-triggered), and a one-shot startup packet.\n\nRatio note: the MainLogicManager click ring's read cursor is NOT advanced by SendEventMouseClick --\nthe main-logic tick advances it itself, once per tick, after this pump returns. The NATIVE sender\nadvances its own cursor inside SendNativeMouseClick. Net effect either way: exactly one entry consumed\nper ring per tick, hence at most one EVENT_MOUSE_CLICK and at most one native packet per tick.
