func=jag::PacketHandlers::UpdateInvPartial	func_addr=0x000fbce0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::PacketHandlers::UpdateInvPartial - handler+0x0 \e jag::Client*.\nWire: g2 inventoryId, g1 flags (bit0 \e secondary inventory, bit1 \e per-slot vars follow).\nGetInventory(client[0x19988], id, flags&1), falling back to CreateInventory.\nThen, while pos < endPos: gSmart1or2 slot; count \e (g_protocolRevision < 0x3B5 ? g2 : g3);\nif count !\e 0 { objId \e g1, and if that byte \e\e 0xFF then g4; if (flags&2) varCount \e g1 }.\nPer var: g2 varId + g4 value, stored via FindOrCreateEntry into inv[0x28] + slot*0x38 + 8.\nTail: dirty-inventory ring on client[0x19958] - int[64] at +0xa8 indexed by (counter++ & 0x3f)\nat +0xb0 (the same manager UpdateStat uses, whose stat ring is at +0xc8/+0xd0).\nEvidence: (1) field-for-field identical decode ladder to Linux UpdateInvPartial, including the\n0xFF count escape and the (flags&2) var loop; (2) same GetInventory-then-CreateInventory pair and\nthe same VarDomain::FindOrCreateEntry destination arithmetic (slot*0x38 + 8); (3) same dirty-ring\ntail and the same handler sentinel return value as UpdateStat.\nOClient: INVENTORY_MANAGER \e 0x19988.
