func=jag::input::EventListeners::DispatchMouseEventWithSource	func_addr=0x00789ae0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::input::EventListeners::DispatchMouseEventWithSource(inputHandler, x, y, message, sourceFlags)\n\nWindows-only. Walks the listener vector at inputHandler+0x828 (begin/end/capacity +0x828/+0x830/+0x838,\nmutex +0x840) and calls each listener's invoker at slot +0x10 with (x, y, message, &sourceFlags) --\nsourceFlags BY POINTER, unlike the per-message slot dispatchers. Stops and returns 1 at the first\nlistener that returns non-zero.\n\nThe client's InputHandler lives at client+0x18E50, so this vector IS client+0x19678 and the sibling\nmove vector at +0x890 IS client+0x196e0.\n\nLISTENER CENSUS (matters for side-effect safety): the ONLY registration into client+0x19678 anywhere\nin .text is jag::ClientProt::Construct, and the only removal is\njag::ClientProt::DestroyNativeMouseProt -- both push/pop the NativeMouseProt's clickListener, whose\ninvoker is jag::ClientProt::RecordNativeMouseButton (a pure ring push). Same for the move vector at\nclient+0x196e0. Verified by scanning .text for the displacements 0x19678 / 0x196e0 / 0x828 / 0x890:\napart from these two functions the only hits are DispatchMouseEventWithSource /\nDispatchMouseMoveWithSource (reads), ~InputHandler and RemoveAllListeners (teardown), plus\nstack-frame false positives. So this dispatch has NO local game side effects. Registration is still\ndynamic, so re-check the census on every build.\n\nsourceFlags is MSLLHOOKSTRUCT.flags carried from the WH_MOUSE_LL hook (installed in FUN_00729d00 via\nSetWindowsHookExA(WH_MOUSE_LL\e0xE, FUN_007292f0), skipped entirely when IsDebuggerPresent()); the\nimmediate caller is jag::input::DispatchLowLevelMouseMessage. Bit 0 is LLMHF_INJECTED.\n\nReached only for button messages: WM_LBUTTONDOWN 0x201, WM_LBUTTONDBLCLK 0x203, WM_RBUTTONDOWN 0x204,\nWM_RBUTTONDBLCLK 0x206, WM_MBUTTONDOWN 0x207, WM_MBUTTONDBLCLK 0x209. There is NO button-UP message in\nthe set. WM_MOUSEMOVE 0x200 goes to DispatchMouseMoveWithSource instead; every other message is\nfiltered out before dispatch.
