func=jag::ClientStream::Read	func_addr=0x00639810	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::ClientStream::Read(this, dst, len) -> bytesRead. Single funnel for ALL raw S->C bytes\n(pre-ISAAC, pre-prot). Engine RawLoginDump hooks this to capture the login/RSA handshake.\nRing buffer fields (int indices on this): +0x78 begin, +0x80 end, +0x90 readPtr, +0x98 writePtr,\n+0xa0 count, +0x0 connected. Socket top-off is outlined into FUN_00639920 (select + ioctlsocket\nFIONREAD + recv), which GCC inlines on Linux.\nEvidence: (1) identical control flow to Linux jag::ClientStream::Read - entry counter increment,\n`(end-begin)\e\e1 -> return 0`, the `avail<len || (cap-1)/10 < (cap-1-avail)` top-off predicate, the\nwraparound drain loop, and the disconnected-and-drained reset; (2) identical ClientStream field\noffsets, cross-checked against GetAvailable/Write/Flush/Close in the same class;\n(3) byte-total global _DAT_00e88a78 accumulated at exit, mirroring the Linux exit accumulator.
