func=jag::game::NPC::NPC	func_addr=0x0039c620	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=NPC ctor. Identified by its sole caller FUN_001af2a0, which allocates from a pool of stride 0x11b0, places the NPC at poolSlot+0x20, and passes entityType \e 1 - the value Entity+0x10 must hold for the NPC branch. PathingEntity's own range ends at 0x1078; every field this ctor writes from param_1[0x20f] (+0x1078) upward is NPC-specific, and the object ends around +0x1178. +0x1078 holds the type pointer passed in by the caller.\nDO NOT import the Linux ONPC offsets. ID 0x1060 / TYPE_ID 0x1064 are inside PathingEntity's range on Windows (the base ctor writes 0x10001 at +0x1060). The NPC block appears shifted by roughly +0x18 relative to Linux, but that is arithmetic, not evidence - none of ID, TYPE_ID, CURRENT_HP, MAX_HP, HIDDEN_MENUOP_FLAGS or SHOW_AS_IMPORTANT has a confirmed Windows offset. Closing them needs a semantic read: the health-bar path for the HP pair, and the highlight_set_npc_show_as_important CS2 opcode handler (which checks entityType \e\e 1 then writes a bool) for the rest.
func=jag::game::AnimationSlot::ServiceLoad	func_addr=0x002ef5b0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=Services one animation slot: resolves the pending seq through the type cache, builds its AnimationWrapper and swaps the pending pair into the active pair. The slot holds two 0x90-apart sub-slots; each is {id at +0x08, wrapper shared_ptr at +0x20 whose object word is +0x28}. The entity's primary slot is based at entity+0xa88, so its active id is 0xa90 and its wrapper shared_ptr base is 0xaa8 with the object at 0xab0.
func=jag::opcode::highlight_set_npc_show_as_important	func_addr=0x001c1340	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::opcode::highlight_set_npc_show_as_important - CS2 opcode handler.\nIdentified by its OWN string literal "highlight_set_npc_show_as_important" (0xb5f820, sole xref).\n\nGates on Entity+0x10 \e\e 1 (entityType NPC - the value NPC::NPC  passes), pops one int\noff the CS2 int stack and stores (v > 0) as a single bool.\n\n\e> ONPC.SHOW_AS_IMPORTANT \e 0x1120 on Windows. CERTAIN, two independent lines:\n   (1) the single bool this handler writes, on a pointer proven to be an NPC by the type gate;\n   (2) jag::game::NPC::NPC  zeroes exactly one byte at +0x1120 (param_1[0x224]).\n\nNOTE FOR FUTURE PORTS: the Linux value is 0x1100 and an earlier pass hypothesised a +0x18 block\nshift (which would have given 0x1118). The real shift is +0x20. The refusal to record the\narithmetic guess was correct - it would have been wrong by 8 bytes and read a neighbouring field.
func=jag::game::MapSquare::MapSquare	func_addr=0x00399730	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::game::MapSquare::MapSquare (ctor). Linux twin  - the two ctors are field-for-field layout-identical through 0x1ec.\nField map proved here: +0x8 graph node; +0x10..0x13 \e 0x6060a (Linux stores bytes: [0x10]\e0xa, [0x11]\e6, [0x12]\e6, [0x13]\e0 -> READY_LO/READY_HI init equal \e "ready"); +0x40 qword \e -1 (0x39979e, Linux 0x4da6f5 - a -1/-1 int32 pair, NOT the mapsquare X); +0x48/+0x50 shared_ptr{counter,obj}; +0x5c \e mapsquare X (0x3997e7); +0x60 \e mapsquare Y (0x3997ea); +0x68/+0x70 \e ClientCompositeData shared_ptr {counter (0x3997f0, refcount bumped at [ctrl+8]), obj (0x3997f8)}; +0x8c \e 1; +0x90 \e 0 (height PRIMARY); +0x98 \e 1; +0xa0 embedded polymorphic sub-object (ctor 0x395a50, 2-byte field at +0xa8, zero-init run from +0xb0, and the mapsquare x/y copied again to +0x1e8/+0x1ec); +0xeb40..0xebc8 zero run incl. LOCATION_CONTAINERS 0xeb80 and height FALLBACK 0xeba0; +0xece0/+0xece4 \e x/y again.\nCORRECTION to the offsets table: OMapSquare.MAPSQUARE_X/MAPSQUARE_Y/COMPOSITE_DATA_COUNTER/COMPOSITE_DATA are 0x5c/0x60/0x68/0x70 - NOT 0x40/0x9c/0xa8/0xb0. The 0x40/0x9c/0xa8/0xb0 values are a 948-2-era migration error; they are wrong on Linux too. Reader evidence at 0x39a419 / 0x39a40e.
