func=jag::ClientProt::FlushMouseProtSender	func_addr=0x001126b0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::ClientProt::FlushMouseProtSender(MouseProtSenderBase *sender) -- generic per-tick driver shared by\nthe EVENT (aggregate+0x10) and NATIVE (aggregate+0x38) mouse senders. Called from\njag::ClientProt::FlushPerTick, EVENT first then NATIVE, once per game tick.\n\nTwo independent stages:\n\nSTAGE 1 (conditional) -- movement-history packet.\n  Gated on vtable slot 0 (HasPending): sender's CLICK ring non-empty OR\n  (clock 0x00e8e498 - sender->lastMoveSampleTime) > 0x7d0. So the history packet is emitted at most\n  every 0x7d0 clock units, or immediately whenever a click is also pending.\n  Loop: slot 4 (PopNativeMouseMoveSample) pops one sample and advances the move ring's read cursor;\n  x/y are clamped to 0..0xfffe with 0xffffffff meaning off-window; samples whose (x,y) equal\n  lastSentX/lastSentY are skipped without being written. Time is delta-encoded as\n  (sample->timestamp - lastMoveSampleTime) / 0x14 with the remainder accumulated and later emitted as\n  average + remainder bytes; the position uses a 1/2/4-byte tiered delta form. Each written sample also\n  calls vtable slot 5, which for the NATIVE sender is\n  jag::ClientProt::WriteNativeMouseMoveSourceByte -- one sample->sourceFlags byte per history sample.\n  The loop stops early when the packet approaches its size budget (slot 3 supplies the headroom).\n  A count byte is back-patched at the end.\n\nSTAGE 2 (unconditional) -- vtable slot 1 (SendEventMouseClick / SendNativeMouseClick) is tail-called\non EVERY invocation, including when HasPending was false. Each Send self-guards on its own click ring\nbeing non-empty, so per tick each sender emits at most one click packet.
