func=jag::ScenePicker::TestEntityHit	func_addr=0x002fbdc0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=Settles the Entity screen-space picking block on Windows. Entity+0x14 selects the mode. Mode 0 (point): +0x30 centre X, +0x34 centre Y, +0x38 radius, circle test dx^2+dy^2 &lt;\e (radius+clickRadius)^2. Mode !\e 0 (line): +0x18/+0x1c endpoint 1, +0x20/+0x24 endpoint 2, +0x28 radius, point-to-segment distance with projection clamped to the segment. Reaches the entity as *(pickable+8) and its GraphNode via Entity+0x8. Entity vtable slots used: +0x20 (unshifted vs Linux), +0x88 IsPickable (Linux +0x90), +0x108 mark-picked (Linux +0x110) - the -8 shift applies to the later slots only, not to +0x20.
func=jag::packethandlers::ClientState::REBUILD_NORMAL	func_addr=0x000f5ea0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=ServerProt op 64 REBUILD_NORMAL (varShort). Bound via the per-opcode ProtEntry array at 0x00e99670 (stride 0x50): entry[64] \e 0x00e9aa70, eastl::function slot at entry+0x10 \e 0x00e9aa80, bound by the binder at 0x000f5200 with functor vtable 0x00b58398 whose invoke slot 0x00108900 is an `add rcx,8; jmp` thunk into this body.\nBody: [g2 playerX][g1 hi,g1 lo(+0x80) playerY][g1 @+6 npcInfoCoordBitWidth -> NpcManager(client+0x198f0)+0xc0e8][g1 @+7 magic MUST\e\e5 else early-out][g2 worldAreaTypeId][g4 packed SW][g4 packed NE]; packed coord \e {x\e(v>>14)&0x3fff, y\ev&0x3fff}, 0xffffffff \e none. Then SceneManager(client+0x19990)::CreateWorldFromWorldArea(FUN_002f5180) over sw>>6 / ne>>6 map squares, camera reset tail.\nCross-checked against jag::PacketHandlers::RebuildNormal  in the Linux 949-1 build (behaviour only).
