func=jag::game::VarDomain::FindOrCreateEntry	func_addr=0x000fda50	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::game::VarDomain::FindOrCreateEntry(domain, int* key) -> &entry.variant (node + 0x8).\nChained hash map: buckets at domain+0x8, bucketCount at domain+0x10, size at domain+0x18,\nallocator at domain+0x20. Node: +0x0 key, +0x8 variant payload, +0x20 variant type tag\n(initialised to 4 \e empty), +0x28 next. Rehashes via FUN_00100e10 when the load policy trips.\nEvidence: (1) same find-or-create-and-return-payload contract as Linux\njag::game::VarDomain::FindOrCreateEntry; (2) called by UpdateInvPartial/UpdateInvFull at exactly\nthe point the Linux handlers call FindOrCreateEntry, with the same slot*0x38+8 destination;\n(3) its result is always fed straight into the variant-assign helper, as on Linux.
