func=jag::ClientProt::RecordNativeMouseButton	func_addr=0x00141470	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::ClientProt::RecordNativeMouseButton -- the eastl::function invoker registered into the\nInputHandler native-mouse-BUTTON listener vector (handler+0x828, \e\e client+0x19678).\n\nrcx is the bound-function object; the NativeMouseProt is at boundFunction+0x8. Args arrive BY POINTER\n(x, y, message, &sourceFlags) exactly as jag::input::EventListeners::DispatchMouseEventWithSource\npasses them.\n\nTHIS IS THE ONLY THING THE BUTTON-WITH-SOURCE DISPATCH DOES. The body is, in order:\n  1. bail out unless connection state \e\e 2 (client+0x19878 -> +0x18 -> +0x8 -> [0]); returns 0\n  2. slot \e &this->clickRing[this->clickRingWrite]\n     slot->x \e (float)*x ; slot->y \e (float)*y\n     slot->timestamp \e *(qword*)0x00e8e498   (the monotonic clock global also read by the\n                                              HasPending predicates; unit inferred as ms from the\n                                              0x14-per-sample divisor in FlushMouseProtSender)\n     slot->message \e *message ; slot->sourceFlags \e *sourceFlags\n  3. clickRingWrite++, wrap to 0 at 10\n  4. if clickRingWrite now \e\e clickRingRead, clickRingRead++ (wrap at 10) -- overflow DROPS the\n     oldest sample rather than refusing the new one\n  5. return 1\n\nNo raycast, no DoAction, no entity-under-cursor, no interface hit-test, no scene query -- nothing but\nthe ring push. The local game-interaction path for a click is entirely separate (WndProc ->\njag::input::Input::On*ButtonDown -> MainLogicManager click ring -> EVENT_MOUSE_CLICK).\n\nThe sibling jag::ClientProt::RecordNativeMouseMove is identical except it targets this->moveRing\n(cursor pair +0x2810/+0x2814, 200 slots) and additionally stores -1 into slot->buttonOrNone.
