func=jag::input::Input::OnRightButtonDown	func_addr=0x0078b8f0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=Input::OnRightButtonDown(Input* this, float x, float y) - name derived by analogy, there is no\nreference symbol (the Linux build has no right/middle button entry point at all; its platform\nadapter writes the state byte and walks the slot inline).\nReached from FUN_0078a2f0 case 0x204 (WM_RBUTTONDOWN) at 0x0078a6d4.\nSets RIGHT_BUTTON_STATE (0x00e8e4f6) \e 1, publishes MOUSE_Y/MOUSE_X, then walks the global\nhandler's RMOUSE_DOWN slot inline: begin handler+0x1a8, end +0x1b0, mutex +0x1c0.\nProves OInputHandler.RMOUSE_DOWN \e 0x1a8 and OInputGlobals.RIGHT_BUTTON_STATE \e 0xe8e4f6.
