func=jag::game::PlayerVarDomain::SetVarBitValueFromServer	func_addr=0x002e97a0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::game::PlayerVarDomain::setBitFromPacket(this, varBitInfo, value) - NOT ::setBit.\nReads the backing varp (varBitInfo->[+0x8]->[+0x40]->+0x8), lazily materialises it when the\nvariant tag is 4, then merges `value` into the bit range [varBitInfo+0x48 .. varBitInfo+0x4c]\nvia mask \e ((1 << (end - start + 1)) - 1) << start, and calls ::set(this, varBitInfo[+8]+0x38, &merged).\nEvidence: (1) the read-modify-write + delegate-to-set shape is unique to Linux\n::setBitFromPacket; Linux ::setBit does no bit merging at all; (2) identical +0x48/+0x4c bit-range\nfield pair and identical mask arithmetic; (3) identical `variant tag \e\e 4` lazy-init branch with\nthe same vtable call.
